<title>JAPAN: Nichimen shares bid-only on share buy-back.</title>
<headline>Nichimen shares bid-only on share buy-back.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Japanese trade house Nichimen Corp were bid-only in early Tuesday trade on news that the company would buy back some of its shares.</p>
<p>As of 0021 GMT, the shares were bid-only at 394 yen, compared with the Monday close of 384 yen.</p>
<p>Nichimen announced after Monday's close that it would buy back up to 150,000 of its own shares, or 1.2 billion yen worth, in order to introduce a stock option scheme.</p>
<p>Stock options give holders the right to buy shares at a set price within a certain period.</p>
